# Download filename branding

Every tool download must use the `focera.co-` prefix before the rest of the filename.

## Required pattern

- Use `downloadBlob` from `@/lib/image` for blob downloads — it applies branding automatically via `brandedDownloadFilename`.
- If you cannot use `downloadBlob` (custom `link.download`, jsPDF `save`, API `Content-Disposition`, etc.), call `brandedDownloadFilename(filename)` from `@/lib/image` before setting the name.
- Do not hardcode the prefix in call sites; do not skip branding for new tools.
- The helper is idempotent — safe if the name already starts with `focera.co-`.

## Examples

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — goes through downloadBlob
downloadBlob(blob, `${fileBaseName(file)}-compressed.pdf`);
// saved as: focera.co-photo-compressed.pdf

// ✅ GOOD — custom download path
link.download = brandedDownloadFilename(`${base}-edited.pdf`);

// ❌ BAD — raw download name without branding
link.download = `${base}-edited.pdf`;
```
